content.text:
Now update main.js imports and logic.

Imports:
```
import { Bot, BOT_DEFS, DOWN_TIME, JakeNPC } from './bots.js';
import { Killer } from './killer.js';
import { Principal } from './principal.js';
import { Cinematic, introShots, lockdownShots, forgotJakeShots, jumpscareShots, jakeRevealShots, policeShots } from './cinematics.js';
```

Constructor add `this.phase='title'` maybe `this._detected=false; this._forgotStarted=false;`.
In init after killer creation:
```
this.principal = new Principal(this);
this.jake = new JakeNPC(this);
```
But Principal constructor imports makeLabel etc. fine.

`startGame`: after intro call `() => this.beginSkip()`.

Add methods to Game prototype in the Object.assign section:
- `beginSkip()`
- `beginLockdown()`
- `beginPlay()` modified (it's defined in constructor class before Object.assign? Actually beginPlay is in class body, yes around line 315. We can edit it in class body and add beginSkip there too, or add in Object.assign. Better add beginSkip/beginLockdown near beginPlay in class body.)
- `onDetected(principal)`
- `startForgotJake()`
- `updateSkip(dt)` maybe integrated in updateGame.

Modify `beginPlay` to support `fromLockdown` flag. Let's design new `beginPlay(fromLockdown=false)`:
```
beginPlay(fromLockdown = false) {
 this.phase='play';
 this.state='play';
 this.setInputActive(true);
 this.world.setLighting('lockdown');
 this.world.setBodiesVisible(false);
 if (!this.killer.active) this.killer.spawn(34,0);
 this.player.pos.set(-4.6,0,-5.2);
 this.player.yaw = Math.PI; // facing south toward door? camera yaw = PI faces +Z (south). yes.
 this.camYaw = Math.PI;
 this.pitch = -0.02;
 ... reset player stats ...
 this.avatar = this.player;
 this.controlledBot=null;
 this.bots.forEach((b,i)=> {
   b.dormant=false;
   b.controlled=false;
   b.model.visible=true;
   const spots = [[-5.2,-1.0],[-2.6,-1.2],[-7.8,-0.7]];
   b.pos.set(...); b.yaw = 0? facing north? 
   ...
 });
 this.principal.setActive(false);
 this.jake.setActive(false);
 ...
 UI.chapter('CHAPTER ONE', "DON'T BE SEEN", 3400);
 this.toast(...)
 ...
 // Jake in the toilet line after 5s
 setTimeout(() => { if (this.phase==='play' && !this.player.dead && !this.player.escaped) { this.radio('JAKE (TOILET)', 'I am guarding the toilets. ...You are coming back, right?'); } }, 5200);
}
```
Player position inside toilet: (-4.6,-5.2), facing south (yaw PI) toward door at z=-3. The toilet interior is z<-3, so camera looks toward door. Good. But the player stands among sinks? Sinks along south wall z2-0.45 = -3.45, x -4.6 (sink1 at x1+2.4 = -4.6). Oops, player at (-4.6,-5.2) is 1.75m north of sink counter, fine. The sink counter is at z=-3.45, not overlapping. Good. But maybe better x=0? Keep.

Bots positions in corridor near toilet: (-5.2,-1.0), (-2.6,-1.2), (-7.8,-0.7). They are in corridor, yaw 0 (facing north? camera?). Fine. They may auto-open doors etc.

`this.player.torchOn = true;` but start in toilet. Good.

Remove the old reset? We'll edit beginPlay fully.

`beginSkip()`:
```
beginSkip() {
 this.phase='skip';
 this.state='play';
 this.inputActive=true;
 this.world.setLighting('day');
 this.world.setBodiesVisible(false);
 this.killer.reset(34,0);
 this.killer.active=false;
 this.principal.spawn(4,0.2,-Math.PI/2);
 // open toilet door so Jake's path works
 const td = this.world.doors.find(d=>d.room.id==='toilets'); td.locked=false; td.setOpen(true,false);
 // player
 this.player.pos.set(-8.0,0,4.15); this.player.yaw=0; this.camYaw=0; this.pitch=-0.02;
 this.player.hp=100; this.player.stamina=100; this.player.battery=100; this.player.torchOn=false;
 this.player.crowbar=false; ...
 this.avatar=this.player; this.controlledBot=null;
 this.jake.spawn(-8.7,0,4.6,0); // behind/beside player
 this.bots.forEach(b=>{ b.dormant=true; b.model.visible=false; b.danger.visible=false; b.state='follow'; });
 this._detected=false;
 UI.hideScreens(); UI.showHud(true); UI.setTouch(this.touch); UI.fade(false,900); UI.letterbox(false); UI.showCine(false);
 UI.chapter('CHAPTER ZERO','SKIP CLASS',3400);
 UI.toast('Reach the toilets with Jake. Do not let Okafor see you.');
 audio.startAmbience(); audio.alarmStop(); audio.chaseStop(); audio.setTension(0.18);
 this.updateObjective(true);
 this.canvas.requestPointerLock?.();
}
```
Player at z=4.15 inside class room. Is that inside the room? Room z1=3,z2=18. Yes. But door at z=3, so player 1.15m from door. Good.
Jake at z=4.6, slightly behind player; he'll path to toilet. Player yaw 0 faces north (toward door). Good.

Wait, the classroom door is at x=-9..-7, so player x=-8 is centered. The door is closed; autoOpenDoors radius 1.7, distance from player (-8,4.15) to door center (-8,3) is 1.15 → opens automatically on first update. That's fine, but then the principal may see the player through the open door? Door opens after first update; principal at x=4,z=0.2 facing west; player at (-8,4.15) inside room, LOS from principal to player passes through doorway? The line from (4,0.2) to (-8,4.15) hits the south wall at z=3 somewhere x≈-4.7, which is wall (door gap -9..-7), so blocked. Good. As player approaches the door at x=-8,z=3.2, LOS passes through doorway. That's when detection could happen. Great.

But `autoOpenDoors` on the player is called in updateGame with radius 1.7; the player may be inside and door opens automatically, revealing them. Fine.

`beginLockdown()`:
```
beginLockdown() {
 if (this.phase !== 'skip' || this.state !== 'play') return;
 this.phase='lockdown';
 this._detected=true? no separate.
 this.principal.setActive(false);
 this.jake.setActive(false);
 this.player.speed=0;
 this.state='cutscene';
 this.setInputActive(false);
 UI.showHud(false); UI.setDetection(false);
 UI.fade(true, 650);
 setTimeout(()=>{
   UI.fade(false, 900);
   this.runCutscene('lockdown', () => lockdownShots(this.cinematic), () => this.beginPlay(true));
 }, 700);
}
```
`runCutscene` sets afterCutscene and calls play, which itself sets state cutscene. Fine.
But `UI.fade(false)` before play; good.

`onDetected(principal)`:
```
onDetected(principal) {
 if (this.phase !== 'skip' || this._detected) return;
 this._detected=true;
 this.phase='detected';
 this.player.speed=0; this.jake.speed=0;
 this.setInputActive(false);
 this.state='cutscene';
 UI.showHud(false); UI.setDetection(false);
 UI.jumpscare(true);
 UI.cineFlash();
 principal.fireLaser(this.player);
 this.shakeScreen(1.2,1.6);
 setTimeout(()=>{
   UI.jumpscare(false);
   UI.caught('DETECTED', 'Principal Okafor\'s eyes are red. The pizza is electric. You are toast.', { kicker:'PRINCIPAL OKAFOR — ELECTRIC PIZZA PROTOCOL', title:'DETECTED', btn:'TRY AGAIN'});
   this.state='caught';
 }, 1650);
}
```
But `UI.cineFlash()` white; add a red overlay. `UI.jumpscare(true)` gives red static; okay.
- Need to make `state='cutscene'` and animate branch updates principal laser. We'll add.
- After `UI.caught`, `state='caught'`. Add animate branch. The caught screen appears above.

Modify `hideGameplayEntities`:
```
if (this.principal) this.principal.model.visible = v ? false : this.principal.active;
if (this.jake) this.jake.model.visible = v ? false : this.jake.active;
```
But `hideGameplayEntities(true)` during intro hides principal (inactive anyway) and Jake. After intro, `hideGameplayEntities(false)` restores Jake to inactive false → hidden. Then beginSkip spawns and shows. Good.

Modify `updateGame(dt)`:
- At top after updateActive:
```
if (this.phase === 'skip') {
  this.jake.update(dt);
  this.principal.update(dt);
} else {
  for bots...
  this.killer.update(dt);
}
```
But bots update dormant returns. During skip we still can update bots (no-op). We need principal update only skip. Also check toilet trigger:
```
if (this.phase === 'skip' && this.player.pos.x > -7 && this.player.pos.x < 1 && this.player.pos.z < -3.3) this.beginLockdown();
```
But `beginLockdown` sets state cutscene during updateGame; after it returns, the rest of updateGame should stop to avoid camera updates? Add:
```
if (this.phase === 'skip') {
  ...
  if (inToilet) { this.beginLockdown(); return; }
}
```
- Also update Jake before player? Fine.
- `this.killer.update(dt)` when idle returns quickly.
- `this.principal.update(dt)` could call onDetected which sets state cutscene; return early.
- `world.autoOpenDoors` for jake handled in Jake class.
- detection UI: principal sets its own danger and game.shake; do we show UI.setDetection? Yes, in principal.update set `UI.setDetection(seen)`? But detection is global for killer. During skip, `updateEffects` will set UI detection false because killer inactive. We can change updateEffects:
```
if (this.phase==='skip' && this.principal) UI.setDetection(this.principal.detect > 0.18);
else if (active && killer.active) ...
```
- Also during skip, `this.updateEffects` plays heartbeat based on proximity (killer inactive so prox 0). Principal shouldn't set `proximity`. Fine.

`updateObjective`: add skip branch.

`finishRun`: modify ending chain.

`startForgotJake` method add.

`startJakeReveal` add fade false and ensure after forgot.

`hideGameplayEntities` update.

`animate`: add `state === 'caught'` branch and principal laser update in cutscene.

`togglePause`: add caught check.

`noise`: during skip, feed principal? Could make principal hear sprinting and turn. Implement `if (this.phase==='skip' && this.principal?.active) this.principal.hear(x,z,radius);` but no hear method. Not necessary.

`getControl` etc. fine.

Also `updateEffects` uses `active && this.killer.active` for detection. Modify.

Also `updateCamera` down check, okay.

`beginPlay` is called after lockdown; phase set play. Need reset `this._detected=false`? No.

`this.killer.reset` in beginSkip sets active false and model hidden. Good.

`this.world.setLighting('day')` in beginSkip; but the intro cinematic shot 4 might leave `UI.cineGradeHide`, etc. finish handles.

Now edits.

