1. check4-front: Jake stands in the hall facing the player. Good. But the classroom door frame is dark brown and quite thick, and the door opens inward? We see a big dark wood panel on the left (the open door leaf) blocking part of the frame. Okay. The "E DOOR OPEN" prompt floats in front of Jake—annoying since the door is already auto-open; the prompt appears because the door is within range and closed? It says "DOOR OPEN", meaning the door is unlocked/open? The prompt likely offers "E DOOR OPEN" when near an unlocked door. Not a problem, but could be removed when the door is already open. Existing behavior maybe.

The bigger issue: Room 101 is a wide room, and turning around shows the class—but the room is huge and sparse because the desk grid is spread; 3 classmates + teacher are visible. The teacher is at the board? In check4-class, the teacher is the dark figure near the blackboard (far wall), and one student in purple (Maya) at a desk, Devon maybe near center, Priya? The shot shows three students? I see purple shirt right, another two near the board? The teacher (brown) and a student dark? Let me look: center-right purple = Maya? She's at (-11.6,8.5), but the view shows her right of center; left of board are two figures: one dark red/black near the board (teacher?) and one brown near the teacher's desk. Hmm. The class is populated enough.

