But the room reads as empty still because only 3 students in a huge room. Add more seated student extras? The intro has 9 students, but the bots are only 3. For gameplay, we could add 3-4 ambient students using makePerson, seated. This would enrich. But performance and scope. The user specifically complained about "empty seniors class"; 3 students + teacher may still read as sparse but not empty. Could spawn 4 more simple students at far desks to fill. Each ~40 meshes; 4 = 160 draw calls in one room, only during chapter zero. Maybe acceptable but the game targets performance. Could reuse low-poly? All makePerson are similar. Better to keep 3+teacher.

Actually, we can add all 5 intro extras as simple seated models with a group and hide when leaving. Given the room appears huge with 9 desk positions, filling 8 is much better. Performance: characters are ~50 meshes each; 8 extra = 400 draw calls. The game already has ~800 props but culled. In Room 101, the culler hides other rooms; 8 characters visible might still be okay on desktop but SwiftShader struggles. Could simplify the extras using a lower-detail model? makePerson has no LOD. Maybe 3 extras enough (total 6 students + teacher). Add 3 in the empty far desks. Let's consider after viewing the class shot: it shows a huge empty foreground/left. The camera is near the door looking south, so the nearest desks (player's and Jake's) are empty; that's expected. The far half has 3 students. Adding 2-3 extras in the middle/far rows would help.

